# ###################
# Docs: Configuration — every arcmoon.config.js key and every JavaScript API option
# ###################
[import = Docs: "@/layouts/Docs.arcm" !]
[import = Code: "@/components/Code.arcm" !]
[import = hl: "@/components/docs/Hl.arcm" !]
[import = Text: "@/components/docs/Text.arcm" !]
[import = Title: "@/components/docs/Title.arcm" !]
[import = Link: "@/components/docs/Link.arcm" !]
[import = List: "@/components/docs/List.arcm" !]
[import = Item: "@/components/docs/Item.arcm" !]

[Docs = slug: "config"]
  [Title = id: "two-ways"]Two ways to set options[end:Title]
  [List]
    [Item][strong]The CLI[end] ([hl = text: "arcm build" !]) reads [hl = text: "arcmoon.config.js" !] from the folder you run it in.[end:Item]
    [Item][strong]The JavaScript API[end] ([hl = text: "new ArcMoon(options)" !]) takes the same names in its options object, plus a few of its own. It doesn\'t read the config file.[end:Item]
  [end:List]
  [Text]Every option is optional: leave one out, and its default is used.[end:Text]

  [Title = id: "config-file"]arcmoon.config.js[end:Title]
  [Text][hl = text: "arcm init" !] creates the config in the current folder. Every option, with its default:[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "js", title: "arcmoon.config.js", text: '
    export default {
      importAliases: { "@": "./src" },   // short names for folders in [import] paths
      removeComments: true,              // leave # comments out of the HTML
      timeout: 5000,                     // ms each page\'s ${ }$ code may run
      bundle: [],                        // npm packages allowed in runtime code
      packages: {},                      // runtime imports loaded from a URL: { dayjs: "https://…" }
      outDir: "./dist",                  // where arcm build writes
      externalScripts: false,            // true: JavaScript in files, not inside the HTML
      externalStyles: false,             // true: CSS in files, not inside the HTML
      assetsDir: "assets",               // folder inside outDir for JS, CSS and url() files
      base: undefined                    // e.g. "/": file URLs from the site root
    };
  ' !]
  [Text]ArcMoon reads it [strong]only from the folder you run [hl = text: "arcm" !] in[end], never from a parent folder. Run [hl = text: "arcm" !] from your project folder. [hl = text: "arcm show config" !] prints what it found.[end:Text]

  [Title = id: "options"]The options[end:Title]
  [Text]Every option is optional: leave one out, and its default is used.[end:Text]

  [Title = size: 3, id: "opt-importAliases"]importAliases[end:Title]
  [Text]Short names for folders, used at the start of [hl = text: "[import]" !] paths. Default: none.[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "js", title: "arcmoon.config.js", text: '
    export default {
      importAliases: { "@": "./src", "~ui": "./src/components" }
    };
  ' !]
  [Code = text: '
    # in any file, however deep
    [import = Card: "@/components/Card.arcm" !]   # → ./src/components/Card.arcm
    [import = Badge: "~ui/Badge.arcm" !]          # → ./src/components/Badge.arcm
  ' !]
  [Text]Targets start from the project folder. Without the alias, a page in [hl = text: "pages/blog/" !] would need [hl = text: "../../src/components/Card.arcm" !]. More in [Link = text: "Import aliases", href: "components.html#aliases" !].[end:Text]

  [Title = size: 3, id: "opt-removeComments"]removeComments[end:Title]
  [Text]Whether [hl = text: "#" !] and [hl = text: "###" !] comments are left out of the HTML. Default: [hl = text: "true" !].[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "js", title: "arcmoon.config.js", text: '
    export default { removeComments: false };
  ' !]
  [Code = text: '
    # Page header
    [h1]Home[end]
  ' !]
  [Code = lang: "html", title: "HTML with removeComments: false", text: '
    <!-- Page header-->
    <h1>Home</h1>
  ' !]
  [Text]With the default, the HTML is just [hl = text: "<h1>Home</h1>", selectColor: 1 !]. Keep comments when they should ship with the page, like a license note. More in [Link = text: "Comments", href: "comments.html#keep" !].[end:Text]

  [Title = size: 3, id: "opt-timeout"]timeout[end:Title]
  [Text]How many milliseconds each page\'s [hl = text: "${ }$" !] code may run, its components included. Default: [hl = text: "5000" !] (5 seconds).[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "js", title: "arcmoon.config.js", text: '
    export default { timeout: 10000 };   // 10 seconds, for pages that fetch a slow API
  ' !]
  [Text]Code that takes longer is stopped: endless loops, timers and pending requests all end, and the build stops with:[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "log", text: '
    ✗ ${ }$ code took longer than 10000 ms and was stopped
      pages/stats.arcm
  ' !]
  [Text]Raise it only if a page really needs the time. A page that hangs usually has a bug, and the timeout is what stops it.[end:Text]

  [Title = size: 3, id: "opt-bundle"]bundle[end:Title]
  [Text]The npm packages runtime code may import. Default: none. Runtime code goes to every visitor, so ArcMoon only bundles packages you list:[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "js", title: "arcmoon.config.js", text: '
    export default { bundle: ["canvas-confetti", "dayjs"] };
  ' !]
  [Code = text: '
    runtime ${ import confetti from "canvas-confetti"; }$
    [button = onclick: runtime ${ () => confetti() }$]Party[end]
  ' !]
  [Text]Install the package first ([hl = text: "npm install canvas-confetti" !]). Without the entry, the build stops:[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "log", text: '
    ✗ runtime import "canvas-confetti" is not listed in bundle (arcmoon.config.js). Add it to bundle to bundle it from node_modules, or to packages to load it from a URL
  ' !]
  [Text]Not needed for [hl = text: "arcmoon/reactive" !], your own [hl = text: ".js" !] files, URL imports, packages used only in [hl = text: "${ }$" !] (they never reach the browser), or CSS [hl = text: "@import" !]s.[end:Text]

  [Title = size: 3, id: "opt-packages"]packages[end:Title]
  [Text]npm names that runtime code loads from a URL instead of bundling them (ArcMoon 1.1). Nothing is installed or downloaded at build time; the visitor's browser loads the URL:[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "js", title: "arcmoon.config.js", text: '
    export default {
      packages: { dayjs: "https://esm.sh/dayjs@1" }
    };
  ' !]
  [List]
    [Item][hl = text: "import dayjs from \"dayjs\"" !] loads [hl = text: "https://esm.sh/dayjs@1" !]; [hl = text: "\"dayjs/plugin/utc\"" !] loads that URL + [hl = text: "/plugin/utc" !].[end:Item]
    [Item]A key can also be a full path, like [hl = text: "\"lit/html.js\"" !]. Values must start with [hl = text: "https://" !].[end:Item]
    [Item]It is the same option the [Link = text: "browser build", href: "browser.html#packages" !] takes.[end:Item]
  [end:List]

  [Title = size: 3, id: "opt-outDir"]outDir[end:Title]
  [Text]The folder [hl = text: "arcm build" !] writes into. Default: [hl = text: "\"./dist\"" !].[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "js", title: "arcmoon.config.js", text: '
    export default { outDir: "./public" };
  ' !]
  [Code = lang: "text", text: '
    arcm build pages/about.arcm
    ✓ pages/about.arcm → public/about.html  14 B
  ' !]
  [Text][hl = text: "-o" !] on the command line wins over it: [hl = text: "arcm build pages/blog -o public/blog" !].[end:Text]

  [Title = size: 3, id: "opt-externalScripts"]externalScripts[end:Title]
  [Text]Where each page\'s JavaScript goes. Default: [hl = text: "false" !], inside the HTML in a [hl = text: "<script>" !].[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "js", title: "arcmoon.config.js", text: '
    export default { externalScripts: true };
  ' !]
  [Code = lang: "text", title: "dist/", text: '
    index.html              <script type="module" src="./assets/index-MTLSBKEV.js">
    assets/
      index-MTLSBKEV.js     this page\'s code
      chunks/
        chunk-E7XXX4QS.js   code shared by pages, like arcmoon/reactive
  ' !]
  [List]
    [Item][strong]Inside (default):[end] one file per page, nothing else to copy. Good for small sites and single pages.[end:Item]
    [Item][strong]In files:[end] shared code is downloaded once and cached across pages. Good for sites with many pages.[end:Item]
  [end:List]

  [Title = size: 3, id: "opt-externalStyles"]externalStyles[end:Title]
  [Text]Where each page\'s CSS goes. Default: [hl = text: "false" !], inside the HTML in a [hl = text: "<style>" !].[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "js", title: "arcmoon.config.js", text: '
    export default { externalStyles: true };
  ' !]
  [Code = lang: "text", title: "dist/", text: '
    index.html              <link rel="stylesheet" href="./assets/index-IH2BDP4O.css">
    assets/
      index-IH2BDP4O.css    all of this page\'s CSS
  ' !]
  [Text]It is separate from [hl = text: "externalScripts" !]: you can have the JavaScript in files and the CSS inside the page, or the other way round.[end:Text]

  [Title = size: 3, id: "opt-assetsDir"]assetsDir[end:Title]
  [Text]The folder inside [hl = text: "outDir" !] for JavaScript and CSS files, and for [hl = text: "url()" !] files copied from CSS. Default: [hl = text: "\"assets\"" !].[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "js", title: "arcmoon.config.js", text: '
    export default { externalScripts: true, assetsDir: "static" };
  ' !]
  [Code = lang: "text", title: "dist/", text: '
    index.html              <script type="module" src="./static/index-QZCVOMHP.js">
    static/
      index-QZCVOMHP.js
  ' !]

  [Title = size: 3, id: "opt-base"]base[end:Title]
  [Text]How pages link to those files. Default: relative to each page ([hl = text: "./assets/…" !]). Set it to the URL where [hl = text: "outDir" !] is served:[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "js", title: "arcmoon.config.js", text: '
    export default { externalScripts: true, base: "/" };
  ' !]
  [Code = lang: "html", text: '
    <!-- default -->
    <script type="module" src="./assets/index-MTLSBKEV.js"></script>
    <!-- base: "/" -->
    <script type="module" src="/assets/index-MTLSBKEV.js"></script>
  ' !]
  [List]
    [Item]Use it when pages are served from paths that don\'t match their files, for example by a server that rewrites URLs.[end:Item]
    [Item]Subfolders built with [hl = text: "-o" !] get their own [hl = text: "assets/" !] ([hl = text: "dist/blog/assets/" !]). When the [hl = text: "-o" !] folder is inside [hl = text: "outDir" !], [hl = text: "base" !] gets that folder: [hl = text: "-o dist/blog" !] with [hl = text: "base: \"/\"" !] links to [hl = text: "/blog/assets/…" !] (ArcMoon 1.1).[end:Item]
  [end:List]

  [Title = id: "api-options"]Options only in the JavaScript API[end:Title]
  [Text]These go in [hl = text: "new ArcMoon({ … })" !] next to the options above. See the [Link = text: "JavaScript API", href: "api.html" !] for [hl = text: "compile()" !] and [hl = text: "build()" !].[end:Text]

  [Title = size: 3, id: "opt-filename"]filename and src[end:Title]
  [Text]The page to build: a file, or the page as a string. Give one of them.[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "js", text: '
    new ArcMoon({ filename: "pages/index.arcm" });
    new ArcMoon({ src: "[p]Hello ${ 2 + 3 }$[end]" });
  ' !]
  [Text]With both, [hl = text: "src" !] is the code and [hl = text: "filename" !] is its name in messages and the folder its imports start from. With [hl = text: "src" !] alone, the page is called [hl = text: "anonymous.arcm" !], in [hl = text: "cwd" !].[end:Text]

  [Title = size: 3, id: "opt-props"]props[end:Title]
  [Text]Data for the page, read with [hl = text: "ArcMoon.props()" !] like a component\'s props. Default: none.[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "js", text: '
    const html = await new ArcMoon({
      filename: "pages/user.arcm",
      props: { name: "Maryan" }
    }).compile();
  ' !]
  [Code = title: "pages/user.arcm", text: '
    ${ const { name } = ArcMoon.props(); }$
    [h1]Hello, ${ name }$[end]
  ' !]
  [Text]Props are copied in as real values (objects, arrays, dates), never turned into text. Use them for one template and many pages, or a server that builds a page per request.[end:Text]

  [Title = size: 3, id: "opt-cwd"]cwd[end:Title]
  [Text]The project folder: where relative paths start. Default: [hl = text: "process.cwd()" !], the folder Node.js runs in.[end:Text]
  [List]
    [Item]A relative [hl = text: "filename" !], and [hl = text: "importAliases" !] targets, start here.[end:Item]
    [Item]A [hl = text: "[script = src: \"/app.js\"]" !] that starts with [hl = text: "/" !] is read from here.[end:Item]
    [Item]Packages in [hl = text: "bundle" !] are found in its [hl = text: "node_modules" !].[end:Item]
  [end:List]
  [Code = lang: "js", text: '
    new ArcMoon({ filename: "pages/index.arcm", cwd: "/home/adam/my-site" });
  ' !]

  [Title = size: 3, id: "opt-root"]root[end:Title]
  [Text]The folder whose files count as yours for the [Link = text: "protector", href: "protector.html" !]. Files outside it are templates, which must be trusted before their code runs. Default: [hl = text: "cwd" !].[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "js", text: '
    // a build script in tools/, for the project one folder up
    new ArcMoon({ filename: "pages/index.arcm", cwd: "..", root: ".." });
  ' !]

  [Title = size: 3, id: "opt-dev"]dev[end:Title]
  [Text][hl = text: "true" !]: the page\'s JavaScript isn\'t minified and has a source map back to the [hl = text: ".arcm" !] lines, so browser errors show real names and lines. Default: [hl = text: "false" !]. The CLI\'s [hl = text: "arcm build --dev" !] sets it.[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "log", text: '
    # with dev: true, a browser error points at the .arcm file
    TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading \'value\')  pages/index.arcm:5:22
  ' !]

  [Title = size: 3, id: "opt-onWarning"]onWarning[end:Title]
  [Text]What to do with each warning. It gets [hl = text: "{ source, position, message }" !]: the file, [hl = text: "{ line, character }" !] counted from 0 (or [hl = text: "null" !]), and the text. Default: print one line, [hl = text: "⚠ page.arcm:3:7  …" !].[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "js", text: '
    // fail a CI build on any warning
    const warnings = [];
    await new ArcMoon({ filename: "pages/index.arcm", onWarning: (w) => warnings.push(w) }).compile();
    if (warnings.length) process.exitCode = 1;
  ' !]
  [Text]Read the three fields; don\'t parse the text, which can change in any release.[end:Text]

  [Title = size: 3, id: "opt-name"]name[end:Title]
  [Text]The page\'s name in [hl = text: "build()" !] and [hl = text: "buildPages()" !]: its entry in [hl = text: "pages" !], and the start of its file names ([hl = text: "post-MTLSBKEV.js" !]). Default: the file name without [hl = text: ".arcm" !], or [hl = text: "page" !] for [hl = text: "src" !].[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "js", text: '
    const pages = posts.map((post) => ({
      filename: "templates/Post.arcm",
      name: post.slug,   // its name in pages[], and the start of its file names
      props: { post }
    }));
  ' !]

  [Title = id: "build-options"]Options of build() and buildPages()[end:Title]
  [Text]These say where files go and how pages link to them. They match the config keys of the same name, with one difference: [strong][hl = text: "externalScripts" !] is [hl = text: "true" !] by default here[end], so JavaScript goes into files. The CLI and [hl = text: "compile()" !] put it inside the page.[end:Text]
  [List]
    [Item][Link = text: "outDir", href: "#opt-outDir" !], [Link = text: "assetsDir", href: "#opt-assetsDir" !], [Link = text: "base", href: "#opt-base" !], [Link = text: "externalScripts", href: "#opt-externalScripts" !] (default [hl = text: "true" !]), [Link = text: "externalStyles", href: "#opt-externalStyles" !]: for [hl = text: "build()" !] and [hl = text: "buildPages()" !].[end:Item]
    [Item][Link = text: "bundle", href: "#opt-bundle" !], [Link = text: "packages", href: "#opt-packages" !], [Link = text: "cwd", href: "#opt-cwd" !], [Link = text: "dev", href: "#opt-dev" !], [Link = text: "onWarning", href: "#opt-onWarning" !]: in [hl = text: "buildPages()" !]\'s second argument, for all pages at once.[end:Item]
  [end:List]
  [Code = lang: "js", text: '
    // one page
    const { html, files } = await new ArcMoon({ filename: "pages/index.arcm" }).build({
      outDir: "dist",
      base: "/"
    });

    // many pages: page options first, then options for all of them
    const { pages } = await buildPages(
      [{ filename: "pages/a.arcm" }, { filename: "pages/b.arcm" }],
      { outDir: "dist", bundle: ["dayjs"] }
    );
  ' !]

  [Title = size: 3, id: "opt-siteDir"]siteDir[end:Title]
  [Text][hl = text: "buildPages()" !] only (ArcMoon 1.1). The site\'s main output folder, when [hl = text: "outDir" !] is a folder inside it: [hl = text: "base" !] then gets that folder. Default: [hl = text: "outDir" !]. The CLI passes your config\'s [hl = text: "outDir" !], so [hl = text: "-o" !] builds link right.[end:Text]
  [Code = lang: "js", text: '
    await buildPages(posts, { outDir: "dist/blog", siteDir: "dist", base: "/" });
    // pages link to /blog/assets/…
  ' !]

  [Title = id: "browser"]In the browser[end:Title]
  [Text]The browser build has options of its own ([hl = text: "files" !], [hl = text: "baseUrl" !], [hl = text: "packages" !], [hl = text: "env" !]…): see [Link = text: "Browser build", href: "browser.html#options" !].[end:Text]
[end:Docs]
